  "prompt": "What is the VAT treatment of the sale of a residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe sale of a residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million is subject to VAT because it exceeds the threshold of ₱1.5 million for residential lots, as stipulated in the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\n- **RR 16-2005**: Implements the VAT provisions and specifies that sales of residential lots exceeding ₱1.5 million are subject to VAT.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, the seller of the residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million must charge VAT on the sale, which is currently set at 12%. This means that the seller will need to compute the VAT based on the selling price and remit this tax to the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). Buyers should also be aware that the total cost will include this VAT, impacting their overall financial commitment in the transaction.",
